cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Inheritance as a Linear Operator, and What Replaces It: From Punnett squares to a complete probabilistic kernel"
abstract: >-
  A unified, audited and extended treatment of Mendelian inheritance modelling.
  An earlier linear-algebra formulation of sickle-cell, ABO and ABO x Rh
  inheritance is preserved and then audited against its own source code, which
  shows that the original programs already enumerated every parental pair and
  that the reported coverage figures describe the prose rather than the executed
  model. The square-matrix constraint is replaced by a complete rectangular
  transmission kernel, implemented in four representations that agree to
  6.94e-17 and benchmarked. Combinatorial growth is proved by induction, and
  output-size lower bounds show that materialising the complete kernel is
  Omega(15^n) for any implementation while the factored single-child query is
  Theta(n) and therefore optimal. Population assumptions are tested against
  public rs334 and rs12913832 genotype calls for 2,504 individuals across 26
  populations. Eye colour is added as a two-locus epistatic trait on real data
  and compared against published cohorts. A final part derives, without
  implementing, an extension in which age enters through germline mutation and
  epigenetic regulation. No predictive accuracy is established for any trait.
type: software
